Codebase Provenance
-------------------

1. Upstream WhiteMatterAnalysis (SlicerDMRI)
   - Source: https://github.com/SlicerDMRI/whitematteranalysis
   - Original Authors: Lauren J. O'Donnell, Fan Zhang, Isaiah Norton, Ye Wu,
     Yogesh Rathi, Nikos Makris, Carl-Fredrik Westin, and contributors
     (Brigham and Women's Hospital, Inc. / SlicerDMRI).
   - Scope: Core diffusion MRI streamline tractography I/O, registration,
     spectral clustering, anatomical outlier removal, tract measurement,
     utilities, and legacy `bin/wm_*.py` CLI scripts (initial repository
     import commits `92c3548..6c0a795`).

2. Initial GPU & Vectorized CPU Acceleration Foundation
   - Source: NeuroDMRI/whitematteranalysis_gpu
   - Author: Yijie Li (`yishengpoxiao`)
   - Scope: Initial PyTorch GPU backend, tiled CPU backend, streaming
     geometry/laterality optimizations, and baseline parity tests/benchmarks.

3. Triton Kernels, Slicer-Free Nonrigid Pipeline, SDK & Packaging
   - Source: https://github.com/xiaji/fast-wma
   - Author: xiaji
   - Scope: Custom 2D Triton kernels (distance, embedding, split-C nearest
     centroids, O(N + R^3) nonrigid B-spline backward, batched kmeans2),
     pure-Python/VTK affine/BSpline/Composite transform hardening,
     zero-intermediate single-process ORG/East-West/NABA parcellation engine,
     `whitematteranalysis.pipelines` Python SDK, unified `wma` CLI, PEP 621
     packaging, multi-target Docker/Apptainer containers, and CI.
